                   |BKB-----------------------------------

|YKOThe |YKBareas|YKO command replaces old handwritten lists of hunting
grounds. It groups cataloged public areas by world and region and shows a
rough level range. Try:

  |YKBareas|YKO                    Browse the full catalog
  |YKBareas level <number>|YKO     Find areas near a level
  |YKBareas search <word>|YKO      Search names, tags, worlds, and regions
  |YKBareas info <number>|YKO      Inspect a result from the latest list

Level ranges are guidance, not guarantees. An area may contain bosses,
puzzles, unusual monsters, or creatures whose levels vary. Explore carefully,
especially when the room description warns you.

Many areas have a waysteward beside their wayshard or entrance. A bright
yellow |YKB[?]|YKO means work is available. Use
|YKBengage waysteward|YKO to review the suggested level, objectives,
prerequisites, and rewards before accepting.

You may accept multiple quests and all of them track automatically.
|YKBmyquests|YKO lists them; |YKBqstatus|YKO shows unfinished objectives.
When every objective is complete, a bright yellow |YKB[!]|YKO appears above
the waysteward. Engage that area's steward again to turn the quest in.

Quest objectives can involve combat, items, rescues, or escorts. Ask friends
for help when you need it, but keep quest solutions off public channels so
other players can discover them for themselves.|000

